# E2E Testing Patterns and Best Practices

## Playwright Locator Strategies

### 1. Prefer Semantic Locators

**✅ Use accessible locators first:**

```typescript
// Good - semantic and stable
const loginButton = page.getByRole('button', { name: 'Login' })
const settingsButton = page.getByRole('button', { name: /settings/i })
const userAvatar = page.getByText(firstLetter).first()

// Good - for specific content
const errorMessage = page.getByText('New passwords do not match')
const successNoty = page.locator('shade-noty', { hasText: 'Account created successfully' })
```

**⚠️ Use CSS/style locators sparingly:**

```typescript
// Acceptable when semantic locators aren't available
const userAvatar = page.locator('[style*="border-radius: 50%"][style*="cursor: pointer"]')
const loginForm = page.locator('shade-login form')

// Avoid overly specific selectors that break easily
// ❌ Bad: page.locator('div.user-menu > div:nth-child(2) > button')
```

### 2. Dynamic Content Locators

Handle dynamic content intelligently:

```typescript
// Generate expected content dynamically
export const login = async (page: Page, username = 'testuser@gmail.com', password = 'password') => {
  // ... login logic ...

  // Verify user is logged in by checking for user avatar (should contain first letter)
  const firstLetter = username.charAt(0).toUpperCase()
  const userAvatar = page.getByText(firstLetter).first()
  await expect(userAvatar).toBeVisible()
}

// Handle dynamic test data
const testEmail = `testuser-${Date.now()}@example.com`
const firstLetter = testEmail.charAt(0).toUpperCase()
const userAvatar = page.getByText(firstLetter).first()
```

## Helper Function Patterns

### 1. Encapsulate Complex Interactions

Create helpers that handle complete workflows:

```typescript
export const logout = async (page: Page) => {
  // Find and click the user avatar (circular div with user's first letter)
  const userAvatar = page.locator('[style*="border-radius: 50%"][style*="cursor: pointer"]')
  await expect(userAvatar).toBeVisible()
  await userAvatar.click()

  // Wait for dropdown menu and click logout - use getByRole for better accessibility
  const logoutButton = page.getByRole('button', { name: /log out/i })
  await expect(logoutButton).toBeVisible()
  await logoutButton.click()

  // Wait for logout to complete and verify login form appears
  const loginForm = page.locator('shade-login form')
  await expect(loginForm).toBeVisible()
}
```

### 2. Navigation Helpers

Create reusable navigation functions:

```typescript
export const navigateToUserSettings = async (page: Page) => {
  // Click on the user avatar to open the menu
  const userAvatar = page.locator('[style*="border-radius: 50%"][style*="cursor: pointer"]')
  await userAvatar.click()

  // Click on Settings option
  const settingsButton = page.getByRole('button', { name: /settings/i })
  await settingsButton.click()

  // Verify we're on the settings page
  const settingsPage = page.locator('user-settings-page')
  await expect(settingsPage).toBeVisible()
}
```

### 3. Assertion Helpers

Create helpers that handle common assertion patterns:

```typescript
export const assertAndDismissNoty = async (page: Page, text: string) => {
  const noty = page.locator('shade-noty', { hasText: text })
  const closeNoty = noty.locator('button.dismissNoty')
  await closeNoty.click()
  await noty.waitFor({ state: 'detached' })
}
```

## Form Testing Patterns

### 1. Form Interaction Best Practices

```typescript
const passwordForm = page.locator('form[data-password-reset-form]')
const currentPasswordInput = passwordForm.locator('input[name="currentPassword"]')
const newPasswordInput = passwordForm.locator('input[name="newPassword"]')
const confirmPasswordInput = passwordForm.locator('input[name="confirmPassword"]')
const updateButton = passwordForm.getByRole('button', { name: /update password/i })

// Fill form fields
await currentPasswordInput.fill('currentPassword')
await newPasswordInput.fill('newPassword123')
await confirmPasswordInput.fill('newPassword123')
await updateButton.click()
```

### 2. Form Validation Testing

Test both client-side and server-side validation:

```typescript
// Test client-side validation
await currentPasswordInput.fill('password')
await newPasswordInput.fill('newPassword123')
await confirmPasswordInput.fill('differentPassword123')
await updateButton.click()

// Should show error message for password mismatch
const errorMessage = page.locator('div', { hasText: 'New passwords do not match' })
await expect(errorMessage).toBeVisible()

// Test server-side validation
await currentPasswordInput.fill('wrongPassword')
await newPasswordInput.fill('newPassword123')
await confirmPasswordInput.fill('newPassword123')
await updateButton.click()

// Should show error notification
const errorNoty = page.locator('shade-noty', { hasText: 'Current password is incorrect' })
await expect(errorNoty).toBeVisible()
```

### 3. Form State Verification

Verify form behaves correctly after operations:

```typescript
// Form should be cleared after successful update
await expect(currentPasswordInput).toHaveValue('')
await expect(newPasswordInput).toHaveValue('')
await expect(confirmPasswordInput).toHaveValue('')
```

## Test Organization Patterns

### 1. Test Structure

Organize tests by feature and user flow:

```typescript
test('User Settings Navigation', async ({ page }) => {
  // Setup
  await page.goto('/')
  await login(page)

  // Action
  await navigateToUserSettings(page)

  // Verification
  const settingsHeading = page.locator('h1', { hasText: 'User Settings' })
  await expect(settingsHeading).toBeVisible()
})

test('Password Reset Functionality', async ({ page }) => {
  // Test complete password reset workflow
})

test('Password Reset Error Handling', async ({ page }) => {
  // Test error scenarios
})
```

### 2. Test Data Management

Use dynamic test data to avoid conflicts:

```typescript
// Generate unique test data
const testEmail = `testuser-${Date.now()}@example.com`
const testPassword = 'testpassword123'

// Use in tests
await usernameInput.fill(testEmail)
await passwordInput.fill(testPassword)
```

### 3. End-to-End Flow Testing

Test complete user workflows:

```typescript
test('Password Reset Functionality', async ({ page }) => {
  await page.goto('/')
  await login(page)

  // Navigate to settings and change password
  await navigateToUserSettings(page)
  // ... password change logic ...

  // Test login with new password by logging out and back in
  await logout(page)

  // Verify new password works
  const loginForm = page.locator('shade-login form')
  await usernameInput.fill('testuser@gmail.com')
  await passwordInput.fill('newPassword123')
  await loginButton.click()

  await assertAndDismissNoty(page, 'Welcome back ;)')
})
```

## Custom Component Testing

### 1. Shadow DOM Components

Handle custom components with shadow DOM:

```typescript
// Test Shades components
const loginForm = page.locator('shade-login form')
const registerForm = page.locator('shade-register form')
const settingsPage = page.locator('user-settings-page')
```

### 2. Component Interaction Patterns

Test complex component interactions:

```typescript
// Avatar dropdown menu interaction
const userAvatar = page.locator('[style*="border-radius: 50%"][style*="cursor: pointer"]')
await userAvatar.click()

// Wait for menu to appear
const settingsButton = page.getByRole('button', { name: /settings/i })
await expect(settingsButton).toBeVisible()
await settingsButton.click()
```

### 3. Component State Testing

Verify component state changes:

```typescript
// Verify dropdown opens
await userAvatar.click()
const dropdownMenu = page.locator('user-avatar-menu button', { hasText: 'Settings' })
await expect(dropdownMenu).toBeVisible()

// Verify dropdown closes after action
await dropdownMenu.click()
await expect(dropdownMenu).not.toBeVisible()
```

## Error Handling and Edge Cases

### 1. Network Error Simulation

Test error conditions:

```typescript
// Test with incorrect credentials
await currentPasswordInput.fill('wrongPassword')
await newPasswordInput.fill('newPassword123')
await confirmPasswordInput.fill('newPassword123')
await updateButton.click()

// Verify error handling
const errorNoty = page.locator('shade-noty')
await expect(errorNoty).toBeVisible()
```

### 2. Validation Error Testing

Test form validation at different levels:

```typescript
// HTML5 validation
await expect(usernameInput).toHaveJSProperty('validity.valid', false)
await expect(usernameInput).toHaveJSProperty('validity.typeMismatch', true)

// Custom validation
const errorMessage = page.getByText('New passwords do not match')
await expect(errorMessage).toBeVisible()
```

### 3. Loading State Testing

Test loading and async states:

```typescript
// Verify button disabled during submission
const submitButton = page.getByRole('button', { name: 'Update Password' })
await submitButton.click()
await expect(submitButton).toBeDisabled()

// Verify loading text
await expect(submitButton).toHaveText('Processing...')
```

## Wait Strategies

### 1. Explicit Waits

Use appropriate wait strategies:

```typescript
// Wait for element to be visible
await expect(loginForm).toBeVisible()

// Wait for element to be detached
await noty.waitFor({ state: 'detached' })

// Wait for network requests (if needed)
await page.waitForResponse('**/api/identity/password-reset')
```

### 2. Avoid Hard Waits

Don't use arbitrary delays:

```typescript
// ❌ Bad
await page.waitForTimeout(1000)

// ✅ Good
await expect(element).toBeVisible()
await element.waitFor({ state: 'visible' })
```

